HOSPITAL APPLICATION DEPLOYMENT ON AWS EKS (2 NODES)

==================================================
STEP 1 - CREATE EC2 (BASTION HOST)
==================================================

Name: bastion-host

OS: Ubuntu 22.04

Instance Type: t3.medium

Storage: 30 GB

Security Group:

SSH      22
HTTP     80
HTTPS    443
Custom   8080

==================================================
STEP 2 - CONNECT EC2
==================================================

ssh -i your-key.pem ubuntu@<PUBLIC-IP>

sudo su

==================================================
STEP 3 - UPDATE SERVER
==================================================

apt update -y

==================================================
STEP 4 - CREATE INSTALLATION SCRIPT
==================================================

nano cluster.sh

Paste:

#!/bin/bash

apt update -y

apt install -y unzip curl

curl "https://awscli.amazonaws.com/awscli-exe-linux-x86_64.zip" -o awscliv2.zip

unzip awscliv2.zip

./aws/install

curl -LO "https://dl.k8s.io/release/$(curl -L -s https://dl.k8s.io/release/stable.txt)/bin/linux/amd64/kubectl"

chmod +x kubectl

mv kubectl /usr/local/bin/

curl --silent --location "https://github.com/weaveworks/eksctl/releases/latest/download/eksctl_$(uname -s)_amd64.tar.gz" | tar xz

mv eksctl /usr/local/bin/

Save:

CTRL + O

ENTER

CTRL + X

==================================================
STEP 5 - RUN SCRIPT
==================================================

chmod 777 cluster.sh

./cluster.sh

==================================================
STEP 6 - VERIFY INSTALLATION
==================================================

aws --version

kubectl version --client

eksctl version

==================================================
STEP 7 - CONFIGURE AWS
==================================================

aws configure

AWS Access Key ID: <YOUR_ACCESS_KEY>

AWS Secret Access Key: <YOUR_SECRET_KEY>

Default Region Name: ap-southeast-1

Default Output Format: json

==================================================
STEP 8 - CREATE EKS CLUSTER
==================================================

eksctl create cluster 
--name mohit-cluster 
--version 1.31 
--region ap-southeast-1 
--nodegroup-name mohit-nodes 
--node-type t3.medium 
--nodes 2 
--nodes-min 2 
--nodes-max 2 
--managed

==================================================
STEP 9 - VERIFY CLUSTER
==================================================

kubectl get nodes

Expected:

2 Worker Nodes Ready

==================================================
STEP 10 - CLONE PROJECT
==================================================

git clone https://github.com/Mohitind241/Hospital-Application.git

cd Hospital-Application

==================================================
STEP 11 - DEPLOY KUBERNETES FILES
==================================================

kubectl apply -f namespace.yaml

kubectl apply -f configMap.yaml

kubectl apply -f secret.yaml

kubectl apply -f pv.yaml

kubectl apply -f pvc.yaml

kubectl apply -f deployment.yaml

kubectl apply -f service.yaml

==================================================
STEP 12 - VERIFY DEPLOYMENT
==================================================

kubectl get pods

kubectl get svc

kubectl get pv

kubectl get pvc

kubectl get all

==================================================
STEP 13 - INSTALL HELM
==================================================

curl https://raw.githubusercontent.com/helm/helm/main/scripts/get-helm-3 | bash

helm version

==================================================
STEP 14 - HELM IMPLEMENTATION
==================================================

helm create hospital-app-chart

cd hospital-app-chart

helm lint .

helm template hospital-release .

helm install hospital-release .

helm list

==================================================
STEP 15 - VERIFY HELM
==================================================

helm list

kubectl get all

==================================================
STEP 16 - ACCESS APPLICATION
==================================================

kubectl get svc

Copy EXTERNAL-IP

Open Browser:

http://<EXTERNAL-IP>

==================================================
STEP 17 - DEMO COMMANDS
==================================================

